  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Conversion of dwelling into four flats (3 X studio and 1 X 3 bed); Single and two storey side extension; Single and two storey rear extension; Alterations and extension to roof to raise ridge height and form rear dormers; Roof lights in front and side roof slopes; External alterations, Private amenity space; Boundary treatment; Bin and cycle stores, Landscaping, Parking to front (Demolition of attached garage and&nbsp;outbuildings at rear)",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed family-sized 3-bedroom dwelling, by reason of its location at first and second floor level and the absence of direct access to a dedicated rear garden, would result in a poor-quality and impractical living environment for future occupiers. The reliance on indirect and convoluted access to a subdivided garden area, &amp;nbsp;requiring&amp;nbsp;occupants to exit their private dwelling and pass through shared internal and external circulation spaces, would fail to provide convenient, secure or genuinely usable private amenity space appropriate for the sole family home. This harm is exacerbated by the fact that it has been demonstrated that a compliant family-sized dwelling could be provided at ground floor level with direct access to the rear garden. The proposal therefore represents a suboptimal and unjustified layout and fails to comply with the objectives for high-quality family housing. As such, the development is contrary to &amp;nbsp;the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3(D7), D3(D10) and&amp;nbsp;D6&amp;nbsp;of the London Plan (2021), Policies GR1,&amp;nbsp;HO1 and HO2 of Harrow’s New Local Plan (2021–2040), the Residential Design Guide SPD (2010) and the Housing Design Standards LPG (2023)."
  ],
